# Build-time environment for the Reachy Mini mobile app.
#
# Vite exposes any variable prefixed with `VITE_` to the client bundle
# via `import.meta.env.VITE_*`. Copy this file to `.env.local` and
# fill in the values you need; `.env.local` is gitignored so secrets
# stay on your machine.
#
# OpenAI access is no longer configured here. The mobile shell mints
# per-user OpenAI Realtime ephemeral keys against the website's
# `/api/openai/ephemeral` endpoint at conversation-start time (see
# `src/features/conversation/engine/ephemeral-key.ts`). The master
# key lives in the website Space's secrets, not in this bundle.

# Override the HF central signaling Space.
# Defaults to the production pollen-robotics instance the fleet
# currently registers against. Useful when developing against a
# staging central or a self-hosted relay.
# VITE_REACHY_CENTRAL_URL=https://pollen-robotics-reachy-mini-central.hf.space

# Override the Reachy Mini website API host. Hosts
# `/api/openai/ephemeral` (and future server-side endpoints the
# mobile shell will consume without a robot in the loop). Defaults
# to the production pollen-robotics website Space. Useful when
# pointing the app at a staging Space that has its own
# `OPENAI_API_KEY` secret for testing.
# VITE_REACHY_WEBSITE_URL=https://pollen-robotics-reachy-mini.hf.space
